## Exercise 4.3
Regress `life_exp` on `elec_access` in the 2019 cross-section (`feols`, robust SEs). Interpret the slope in one sentence (units!), give $R^2$ and N, and say what you would worry about before reading it as an effect of electrification.
:::

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Solution

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
m_el <- feols(life_exp ~ elec_access, data = cs, vcov = "hetero")
summary(m_el)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
OLS estimation, Dep. Var.: life_exp
Observations: 198
Standard-errors: Heteroskedasticity-robust 
             Estimate Std. Error t value  Pr(>|t|)    
(Intercept) 51.190996   1.910049 26.8009 < 2.2e-16 ***
elec_access  0.249839   0.020813 12.0039 < 2.2e-16 ***
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1
RMSE: 5.19318   Adj. R2: 0.575036
